  THRESHOLD  k_B T* = 0.1175  (attained at tau = 1.263)

  The manuscript's statement is therefore true exactly when
      k_B T  >=  0.117   in units of the Hamiltonian couplings,
  which are dimensionless draws from U(-1,1) and U(-0.5,0.5). At the
  hardcoded k_B T = 1.0 the claim holds with 8.5x margin;
  below k_B T = 0.117 it fails and the figure's conclusion reverses.

  Quote the threshold, not the inequality. The inequality alone is true by
  choice of an undefined scale and says nothing about the protocol.
